WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:05.542
OSINT is disciplined intelligence work using lawfully accessible public information.

00:00:05.542 --> 00:00:10.603
Raw data and collected facts are not automatically intelligence.

00:00:10.603 --> 00:00:18.073
Intelligence answers a defined question through organized collection, source evaluation, analysis, validation, and reporting.

00:00:18.073 --> 00:00:22.651
Begin with a clear requirement and permitted scope.

00:00:22.651 --> 00:00:31.567
Select source categories that fit the question, preserve provenance, and stop collecting when the need is met.

00:00:31.567 --> 00:00:40.483
Search engines, websites, records, news, technical data, repositories, social sources, imagery, and maps all require context-specific evaluation.

00:00:40.483 --> 00:00:44.579
Corroborate important claims through genuinely independent evidence.

00:00:44.579 --> 00:00:49.639
Examine origin, timeliness, bias, access, expertise, and manipulation risk.

00:00:49.639 --> 00:00:58.555
Distinguish direct observations from source claims and analytical judgments, and communicate confidence without pretending uncertainty has disappeared.

00:00:58.555 --> 00:01:06.507
Document methods, URLs, timestamps, preserved artifacts, transformations, and reasoning so the work can be reviewed.

00:01:06.507 --> 00:01:11.085
Apply privacy, proportionality, access limits, and retention discipline.

00:01:11.085 --> 00:01:18.073
Public visibility never excuses harassment, doxxing, stalking, deception, unauthorized access, or unlawful surveillance.

00:01:18.073 --> 00:01:22.170
The goal is not to collect everything.

00:01:22.170 --> 00:01:31.086
The goal is to answer an important question responsibly and provide useful intelligence to an authorized audience.

00:01:31.086 --> 00:01:40.965
Strong OSINT is careful about evidence, honest about limitations, and focused on decisions that are ethical, lawful, and defensible.
